// Eldr's render settings, the one list of them: renderDelegate.h makes a token
// per setting (HdVkRenderSettingsTokens->name is "eldr:name"),
// GetRenderSettingDescriptors a descriptor, usdview's settings window and
// Houdini's Eldr tab (houdini/gen_ui.py) their groups, from this file.
// docs/settings.md has a row per setting in this order, under a heading per
// group, with the type and default (ctest docs checks).
//
// HDVK_GROUP(title, open): a group; open ones show unfolded in the UIs.
// HDVK_SETTING(name, label, default):
//   label: usdview's. Title Case name, then at most a short "(...)" with the
//     unit or range (explanations and Karma twins go in docs/settings.md,
//     the tooltips). Houdini drops the "(...)", makes "(a, b, c)" of a
//     string a menu and "(lo-hi)" of a number a soft range.
// Groups by topic: the open ones (Sampling ... Viewport) hold the switches,
// "Advanced: <topic>" the knobs of the same topics, then the rest folded.
//   default: a C++ expression for the VtValue, its type the setting's
//     (frame is vkr::Renderer::Frame{}, defaults its post, volume its volume).
// HDVK_VDB_SETTING: only in builds with OpenVDB (HDVK_VOLUMES).

